 Vedanta Aluminium: Nomura maintains 'Buy', sees target price of Rs 500 after marginal Q2 EBITDA beat
 Vedanta Aluminium aims to achieve an EBITDA run rate of $5 billion by the end of FY27, supported by prevailing LME aluminium prices, an improving value-added product mix and expected cost levels.
 Moneycontrol News 
 October 29, 2026 / 10:42 IST 
 --> 
 Nomura values the stock at 5.5 times enterprise value to EBITDA 
 Nomura has maintained its 'Buy' rating on Vedanta Aluminium with a target price of Rs 500, citing a marginal beat in second-quarter EBITDA driven by better-than-expected realisations. 
 The company reported EBITDA of Rs 10,110 crore for Q2FY27, down 2% quarter-on-quarter but 2% above Nomura's and consensus estimates. Aluminium volumes stood at 649 kilotonnes, up 5% year-on-year and in line with the brokerage's estimates. 
 Blended realisations declined Rs 125 per tonne sequentially to $3,510 per tonne, primarily due to lower London Metal Exchange (LME) aluminium prices during the quarter. LME aluminium prices averaged $3,228 per tonne, down 9% quarter-on-quarter. However, realisations were 4% above Nomura's estimates, supported by a favourable value-added product mix. 
 Aluminium cost of production (CoP) per tonne increased 1% sequentially as inflationary pressures on carbon and fuel oil offset structural benefits in alumina costs. The figure was largely in line with the brokerage's estimate. Aluminium EBITDA per tonne declined 9% quarter-on-quarter to $1,646, primarily due to lower realisations, but was 6% above estimates. 
 Management indicated that aluminium CoP per tonne could increase around 4% sequentially in Q3FY27, primarily due to planned power plant shutdowns and higher carbon costs. Despite the near-term pressures, the FY27 cost guidance remains unchanged at $1,650-1,700 per tonne. 
 The Sijimali bauxite mine received consent to operate in September 2026 and is expected to progressively replace imported bauxite, generating estimated cost savings of around $25 per tonne of bauxite. The company targets production of 1 million tonnes from the mine in FY27, scaling up to 5 million tonnes by FY28. 
 Expansion plans and $5 billion EBITDA ambition 
 The company is evaluating a greenfield expansion to increase aluminium capacity to 3 million tonnes and alumina capacity to 6 million tonnes, with land acquisition for the projects in advanced stages. 
 Vedanta Aluminium aims to achieve an EBITDA run rate of $5 billion by the end of FY27, supported by prevailing LME aluminium prices, an improving value-added product mix and expected cost levels. 
 Nomura values the stock at 5.5 times enterprise value to EBITDA and said it currently trades at 4 times one-year forward EV/EBITDA. 
